# Code owners for Holotable.
#
# Listed paths require a review from the owner before merge. The point is not
# process for its own sake: these are the files where a quiet regression stops
# being a bug and starts being a vulnerability. See SECURITY.md and
# docs/src/content/docs/architecture/invariants.md.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                               @jbouder

# The SQL guard. Everything the model emits passes through here: one SELECT
# built from allowlisted parse-tree constructs, the catalog allowlist, the
# function denylist, row and time limits, read-only execution.
/src/lib/sql/                   @jbouder

# The PromQL guard (#384), the same guard for a Prometheus source: one
# expression built from allowlisted parse-tree nodes, the metric allowlist,
# the @ modifier refused, bounded ranges, and the variable and tenant-matcher
# rewrites verified by re-parse.
/src/lib/promql/                @jbouder

# Row-level filters at the edges: which tenant's value a viewer's queries and
# pollers are narrowed to. A wrong binding serves one tenant another's rows.
/src/lib/row-scope.ts           @jbouder

# Dashboard variables: which values a viewer may bind, and the query that
# decides it. A value allowed here that should not be is another tenant's row
# or a value the dashboard never offered.
/src/lib/variables.ts           @jbouder
/src/lib/variable-selection.ts  @jbouder

# Authentication and authorization. OIDC session handling, claim parsing
# (highest role wins, fail-closed), and the central can() check.
/src/lib/auth/                  @jbouder

# The shared IR — the contract between model output, API validation,
# persistence, and the client. A change here changes all four.
/src/lib/ir.ts                  @jbouder

# The upgrader chain every stored spec is read through. A wrong upgrader
# rewrites every saved dashboard as it is read.
/src/lib/ir/                    @jbouder

# Server-side time resolution and range injection. The server, not the client
# or the model, decides what window a panel actually queries.
/src/lib/time.ts                @jbouder

# The source registry: safe connection config and catalog.
/src/lib/registry.ts            @jbouder

# Source credential resolution: which workspace may use which secret_ref, and
# where the credentials are read from. A regression here lets one workspace
# connect with another's database role.
/src/lib/secrets/               @jbouder

# The guard on a model base URL typed into the app (#331): which addresses the
# server will send a request carrying a key to. Loosening it is SSRF.
/src/lib/ai/base-url.ts         @jbouder
/src/lib/ai/guarded-fetch.ts    @jbouder

# The /api/metrics gate. A scrape names dashboards and sources, per-workspace
# model spend, and what the SQL guard is rejecting, and it sits outside the
# session cookie — so loosening this file is a disclosure, not a config change.
/src/lib/metrics-access.ts      @jbouder

# Security policy, contributor expectations, and the license.
/SECURITY.md                    @jbouder
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @jbouder
/LICENSE                        @jbouder
/NOTICE                         @jbouder

# CI and repository automation.
/.github/                       @jbouder
